Z||000000||DjKid||08-02-2000||02:04 PM||||okey, question.. could I buy a catback system for v6 and use it (with minor mods) on a 4banger?<P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Megafiero||08-02-2000||02:14 PM||||Yes, you should have no problems, my friend put my old 85' GT exhaust on his 84'.  The only bit of work is hanging the right exhaust tip, since there was never one there.  Just a little work with the hangers, not to bad at all.<P>Megafiero<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BellaFiero||08-02-2000||03:11 PM||||Not sure if this is the answer you're looking for, but I put a 1988 GT Fiero's exhaust on my 1988 Coupe. It actually bolted on quite easily - I had to buy some universal hangars for the tips, but it looks good. My rear fascia accepted the pipes on the other side quite easily - looks factory! I'm not sure if that works for all coupes, but on my 88 it was rather simple. Took about two hours to install, including taking the old exhaust off. I hope this helps. ||||reg||10
